ghbors", "args": {"node": 959, "window": [60574, 62074]}, "result_digest": "813c0c82f98ec25e", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"both\", \"n_neighbors\": 5, \"neighbors\": [184, 338, 493, 785, 1348], \"node\": 959, \"window\": [60574, 62074]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 41969, "tokens_after": 41969, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_107b45e5", "decision": "present", "mechanism": "regime_switch", "entities": [114, 140, 182, 293, 356, 654, 731, 959, 1107, 1260, 1268, 1311], "window": [55074, 65074], "confidence": 0.88, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_17", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_18", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_19", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_20", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_21", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_22", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_23", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_24", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_25", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_26", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_27", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_28", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_29", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_30", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_31", "role": "support"}], "narrative": "Candidate change point ~t=60074. With a 5000-unit half-window, every sampled group member's contact set flips essentially completely: e.g. node 114 talks to {63,116,239,918,926,1110,1526,1760,1792,1922} in [55074,60074] and to {40,184,493,515,785,897,1245,1505,1750} in [60074,65074] (Jaccard = 0); nodes 356, 140, 731, 1268, 959 all switch from the same old cohort {61,63,116,239,349,749,912,918,926,1110,1526,1593,1760,1792,1922} to the same new cohort {40,80,184,250,327,338,493,515,785,897,924,1348,1355,1505,1750}. The turnover is not gradual: the old partners persist across [45074,50074] and [50074,55074] (stable overlap), the new partners persist across [65074,70074] and [70074,75074], and the group is nearly silent in the narrow interval [59074,61074] (1 event per 1000 units versus ~30) \u2014 a sharp hinge rather than diffuse drift. Volume is flat across the period (~200 events per 5000 units) and total degree is similar for all members, so activity/popularity cannot explain the swap; comparably active non-group hubs (524, 636) show ordinary partial turnover without a synchronized cohort-wide replacement."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_107b45e5\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [114, 140, 182, 293, 356, 654, 731, 959, 1107, 1260, 1268, 1311],\n  \"window\": [55074, 65074],\n  \"confidence\": 0.88,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_29\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_30\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_31\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Candidate change point ~t=60074. With a 5000-unit half-window, every sampled group member's contact set flips essentially completely: e.g. node 114 talks to {63,116,239,918,926,1110,1526,1760,1792,1922} in [55074,60074] and to {40,184,493,515,785,897,1245,1505,1750} in [60074,65074] (Jaccard = 0); nodes 356, 140, 731, 1268, 959 all switch from the same old cohort {61,63,116,239,349,749,912,918,926,1110,1526,1593,1760,1792,1922} to the same new cohort {40,80,184,250,327,338,493,515,785,897,924,1348,1355,1505,1750}. The turnover is not gradual: the old partners persist across [45074,50074] and [50074,55074] (stable overlap), the new partners persist across [65074,70074] and [70074,75074], and the group is nearly silent in the narrow interval [59074,61074] (1 event per 1000 units versus ~30) \u2014 a sharp hinge rather than diffuse drift. Volume is flat across the period (~200 events per 5000 units) and total degree is similar for all members, so activity/popularity cannot explain the swap; comparably active non-group hubs (524, 636) show ordinary partial turnover without a synchronized cohort-wide replacement.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 50868, "total_output_tokens": 6233, "total_tokens": 57101, "total_latency_ms": 88250, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}